WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.566 --> 00:00:03.166
[music]

2
00:00:05.733 --> 00:00:09.100
[Instructor] Great, now our Player
character animations

3
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.966
are in a really good place.
We have our Running animations,

4
00:00:12.333 --> 00:00:14.800
and then when we jump,
you can see we jump for joy,

5
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.566
but we have this weird little issue
where when we jump,

6
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.033
the animation stops short,

7
00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:22.733
and then we start running in the air,

8
00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:24.933
which doesn't really look right.

9
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:27.466
So we're actually going to go

10
00:00:27.466 --> 00:00:30.000
into our "Running_Jump" animation,

11
00:00:31.533 --> 00:00:35.233
and similarly to how we set
the "Speed"

12
00:00:35.233 --> 00:00:37.833
to be a little bit faster
for the run

13
00:00:37.833 --> 00:00:40.000
to just make it look like
the Player's running faster,

14
00:00:41.466 --> 00:00:45.000
we're going to set our animation
Speed just a bit slower.

15
00:00:45.933 --> 00:00:48.266
We'll do a 0.7,

16
00:00:48.266 --> 00:00:51.533
just so that the animation now runs
just a bit longer,

17
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.666
instead of faster,
so when we press Play,

18
00:00:57.533 --> 00:01:01.400
now when we jump,
the animation definitely works

19
00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.466
a lot better; it lasts a bit longer.

20
00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:09.000
I think one thing that we're going to do

21
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.300
just to make it look
a little bit more realistic

22
00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:13.733
is we're actually going to go
into our Player Object,

23
00:01:14.766 --> 00:01:17.666
and we're going to Play around
with some of the variables,

24
00:01:17.666 --> 00:01:19.666
so specifically our "Mass,"

25
00:01:20.066 --> 00:01:22.200
our "Jump Force," 
and our "Gravity Modifier"

26
00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.966
to just make it look
a lot more realistic,

27
00:01:25.066 --> 00:01:27.500
and better for what we want it to be.

28
00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:32.266
So our Mass on our Rigidbody
is a little low.

29
00:01:32.766 --> 00:01:35.233
People don't normally
weigh just 1 kilogram,

30
00:01:35.233 --> 00:01:37.566
so we're going to change our Mass.

31
00:01:38.266 --> 00:01:41.633
Usually, on average, a person
weighs about 60 kilograms or so,

32
00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:44.400
so we'll see what
that does when we press Play.

33
00:01:47.333 --> 00:01:49.700
And we have the jumping animation,
but we don't really,

34
00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:51.700
we don't really go anywhere.

35
00:01:52.066 --> 00:01:54.233
So let's play around
with the Jump Force a little bit.

36
00:01:54.233 --> 00:01:56.233
Maybe let's edit to...

37
00:01:56.533 --> 00:01:59.733
a little bit over,
like 10 times the actual Mass.

38
00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.966
So we'll do like a 700.
We'll see how that looks.

39
00:02:06.866 --> 00:02:08.866
Ooh, I got it a little bit high.

40
00:02:11.233 --> 00:02:13.400
So maybe, let's see,

41
00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:17.266
if we go to our Gravity Modifier,
let's make it a little bit,

42
00:02:17.266 --> 00:02:20.566
let's make it a little bit more.
Let's make it like a 1.5.

43
00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:26.700
And now when we jump,

44
00:02:28.166 --> 00:02:30.166
not bad...

45
00:02:30.866 --> 00:02:34.200
Pretty close. So we could probably 
fiddle with these values a bit more,

46
00:02:34.533 --> 00:02:36.333
but it looks pretty good.

47
00:02:36.333 --> 00:02:38.666
We get pretty close to the Ground
before we start running.

48
00:02:40.466 --> 00:02:42.800
So now what you're going to do is

49
00:02:43.233 --> 00:02:45.666
in your Player Animator window,

50
00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:48.666
if you go to the Jumping Layer,

51
00:02:49.166 --> 00:02:51.966
and then we click on the Running_Jump.

52
00:02:52.566 --> 00:02:55.733
So we'll set the animation
Speed to be a little bit slower.

53
00:02:55.733 --> 00:02:57.733
So I set mine to 0.7.

54
00:02:58.833 --> 00:03:00.866
And then on our Player Object,

55
00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:05.233
we're going to make
the Player weigh a bit more,

56
00:03:05.233 --> 00:03:08.200
so let's make it about
60 or so kilograms.

57
00:03:08.933 --> 00:03:12.966
We pushed up the Jump Force
up to 700.

58
00:03:13.833 --> 00:03:16.766
And then we increased
Gravity just a little bit,

59
00:03:17.433 --> 00:03:20.433
so we set it to about 1.5
so the Player falls

60
00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:22.833
a little bit faster when they reach
the Ground.

61
00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:25.400
Now it's your turn.

62
00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:28.166
[music]
